## Re-discovery trap update

The notes already warn that "move WebglAddon after open()+fit()" keeps being re-proposed in isolation. Add a parallel warning: "re-rasterize on every visibility-class signal we can name" keeps being re-proposed in isolation. Each layer covers a different gap:

* v0.32.0 — webfont-before-open (cold-start measurement)

* v0.32.1 — startup window of corrections (DPR/geometry settle)

* v0.32.2 — post-startup `fit()` sites (resize / font change / reattach)

* v0.32.3 — visibility / focus / 30 s heartbeat (long idle, GPU eviction)

* v0.32.3+PR — `isActive` false→true (task-tab switch reveal)

All five together. None in isolation. Anyone re-proposing one of these as a bare fix has missed the layered nature of the bug.
